    {"move": "EMPIRICAL CHALLENGE", "target": "AN-28", "detail": "Address the prior-turn feedback on attestation maturity directly rather than asserting it. Concede the technology has real deployment gaps — but pivot to a tiered burden that defuses the chip-vendor-moat objection (AN-28, AN-22): attestation is the price of liability IMMUNITY, not a precondition of deployment. A small developer who cannot attest is not penalized with an automatic adverse inference; they simply lack safe-harbor and are judged under ordinary negligence — the doctrine the Accelerationist (AN-14) already says suffices. The moat objection assumes attestation is mandatory for all; condition it on the safe-harbor election and the disparity disappears."},
